From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:46:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] util/disk_cache: multi-file shader cache on Windows

Mesa's disk cache had no Windows implementation (disk_cache_os.c: "TODO:
implement disk cache support on windows") and meson refused
-Dshader-cache on Windows, so NVK on Windows compiled every shader again
in every process: a DXVK game started with seconds of compile stalls on
each launch.

Implement the multi-file cache (the default type) for Windows:

- directory: MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR, else %LOCALAPPDATA%, else %TEMP%,
  plus mesa_shader_cache; paths may use '\' as well as '/';
- the index (shared size counter and key table) is a file mapping, which
  other processes see like the MAP_SHARED mmap;
- an entry is written to <name>.tmp through a handle that shares nothing
  (the flock), then renamed in place while still open
  (SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo), never replacing), or
  deleted on close if another process won;
- entries are read with FILE_SHARE_DELETE so eviction can delete them;
- eviction deletes the least recently used tenth of a random two-hex
  subdirectory, or of the next one that has files (FindFirstFile);
- size accounting uses 4 KiB clusters.

The single-file (Fossilize) and database caches stay unimplemented on
Windows; their open functions already fail there.

Builds without zlib and zstd (the MinGW cross build) store entries
uncompressed instead of failing to configure.

meson: shader-cache is auto-disabled on Windows instead of refused, so
other Windows builds (MSVC, dozen) are unchanged; -Dshader-cache=enabled
turns it on.
---
 meson.build              |   6 +-
 src/util/compress.c      |  38 ++++
 src/util/compress.h      |   2 +-
 src/util/disk_cache.c    |  12 +-
 src/util/disk_cache_os.c | 410 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/util/disk_cache_os.h |   8 -
 6 files changed, 451 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 1d818fc..8f809e4 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1242,8 +1242,10 @@ if with_split_debug.allowed() and get_option('debug')
   add_project_link_arguments('-Wl,--gdb-index', language : ['c', 'cpp'])
 endif
 
+# On Windows, only the multi-file cache is implemented; ask for it with
+# -Dshader-cache=enabled.
 with_shader_cache = get_option('shader-cache') \
-  .require(host_machine.system() != 'windows', error_message : 'Shader Cache does not currently work on Windows') \
+  .disable_auto_if(host_machine.system() == 'windows') \
   .allowed()
 
 if with_shader_cache
@@ -1893,7 +1895,7 @@ endif
 with_compression = dep_zlib.found() or dep_zstd.found()
 if with_compression
   pre_args += '-DHAVE_COMPRESSION'
-elif with_shader_cache
+elif with_shader_cache and host_machine.system() != 'windows'
   error('Shader Cache requires compression')
 endif
 
diff --git a/src/util/compress.c b/src/util/compress.c
index 1f4b429..39fc9cd 100644
--- a/src/util/compress.c
+++ b/src/util/compress.c
@@ -166,4 +166,42 @@ util_compress_inflate(const uint8_t *in_data, size_t in_data_size,
 #endif
 }
 
+#elif defined(ENABLE_SHADER_CACHE)
+
+/* No zlib or zstd (Windows cross builds): the shader cache stores entries
+ * as they are.
+ */
+
+#include <string.h>
+
+#include "util/compress.h"
+
+size_t
+util_compress_max_compressed_len(size_t in_data_size)
+{
+   return in_data_size;
+}
+
+size_t
+util_compress_deflate(const uint8_t *in_data, size_t in_data_size,
+                      uint8_t *out_data, size_t out_buff_size)
+{
+   if (in_data_size > out_buff_size)
+      return 0;
+
+   memcpy(out_data, in_data, in_data_size);
+   return in_data_size;
+}
+
+bool
+util_compress_inflate(const uint8_t *in_data, size_t in_data_size,
+                      uint8_t *out_data, size_t out_data_size)
+{
+   if (in_data_size != out_data_size)
+      return false;
+
+   memcpy(out_data, in_data, in_data_size);
+   return true;
+}
+
 #endif
